# CodeRabbit review conventions

**Why this file:** [CodeRabbit](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/) runs on PRs using [`.coderabbit.yaml`](../../.coderabbit.yaml) (`inheritance: false`, automatic review, `path_instructions`, assertive profile, `enable_prompt_for_ai_agents`). This rule does **not** replace that config — it tells Cursor agents to treat the same YAML + [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) as the source of truth so local work matches what the bot will review.

**Review-only contract:** CodeRabbit is automatic review/comment input, not the merge-readiness gate. The repo config disables write-producing finishing touches: generated docstrings, generated unit tests, simplify, and custom recipes. Do not trigger `@coderabbitai autofix`, `@coderabbitai autofix stacked pr`, `@coderabbitai generate unit tests`, `@coderabbitai generate docstrings`, `@coderabbitai simplify`, or `@coderabbitai run ...` unless the user explicitly asks for that exact action.

**Before PR:** Fix high-confidence actionable comments when a CodeRabbit review actually runs; otherwise run local independent sub-agent review, keep diffs small, and run the allowed `npm run` checks from AGENTS.md. CodeRabbit blocks only while a review is actively running/pending or when completed actionable comments exist. CodeRabbit no-start/skipped/rate-limit/credit/auth/service failure is not a blocker unless repository policy explicitly requires it.

**Historical note:** Old CodeRabbit-heavy plans were written around API-limit and credit-limit failures. Do not use them as current best practice. Prefer the current repo contract: automatic CodeRabbit comments plus local independent bug/persona review.

**Commit status:** If CodeRabbit rate limits or credits are making GitHub red, disable its status with `reviews.commit_status: false`. Do not rely on `fail_commit_status: false` alone while `commit_status` remains enabled.

**Stack specifics** live in other rules — do not duplicate them here: `nextjs-node-server-2026.mdc`, `next-intl-single-locale-routing.mdc`, `react-form-events.mdc`, `ui-color-tokens.mdc`, `admin-list-usability.mdc`, `tdd.mdc`, `e2e-verification.mdc`.

**CodeRabbit config:** [`.coderabbit.yaml`](../../.coderabbit.yaml) `path_instructions` include URL-shape guidance (default no `trailingSlash`; use `/path#hash` not `/path/#hash` for assertions and in-app links) so the bot does not repeat mistaken `/ratings/#…` review suggestions.
